        "root_concepts": "[interpretation]",
        "section": "translation",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Simultaneous and Consecutive Interpretation",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "THE PARADOX:\n  The fastest speakers cause the most errors —\n  but the interpreter has no control over speech rate.\n  This is why conference organizers and interpreters\n  sometimes negotiate speaker rate limits."
    },
    {
      "id": "07-INTERPRETATION.md#025",
      "path": [
        "07-INTERPRETATION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:translation:07-interpretation, git-history:translation:07-interpretation]",
        "canonical_path": "translation/07-INTERPRETATION.md",
        "concepts": "[interpretation]",
        "current_path": "translation/07-INTERPRETATION.md",
        "id": "maxim:translation:interpretation",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "translation",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[interpretation]",
        "section": "translation",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Simultaneous and Consecutive Interpretation",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "BOUNDED-RESOURCE SCHEDULING — THE FORMAL MODEL:\n  Gile's model is a bounded-resource scheduling problem.\n  The constraint: L + M + P + C ≤ Available Capacity.\n  This is formally identical to:\n    CPU scheduling: total CPU demand ≤ available CPU time\n    Bandwidth allocation: Σ(flow demands) ≤ link capacity\n    Thread pool management: work queue depth ≤ pool size × time"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-INTERPRETATION.md#026",
      "path": [
        "07-INTERPRETATION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:translation:07-interpretation, git-history:translation:07-interpretation]",
        "canonical_path": "translation/07-INTERPRETATION.md",
        "concepts": "[interpretation]",
        "current_path": "translation/07-INTERPRETATION.md",
        "id": "maxim:translation:interpretation",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "translation",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[interpretation]",
        "section": "translation",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Simultaneous and Consecutive Interpretation",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The interpreter is a single-threaded system with limited\n  working memory (buffer). The demands on the buffer\n  (incoming speech, held memory, outgoing production)\n  compete for a shared resource."
    },
    {
      "id": "07-INTERPRETATION.md#027",
      "path": [
        "07-INTERPRETATION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:translation:07-interpretation, git-history:translation:07-interpretation]",
        "canonical_path": "translation/07-INTERPRETATION.md",
        "concepts": "[interpretation]",
        "current_path": "translation/07-INTERPRETATION.md",
        "id": "maxim:translation:interpretation",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "translation",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[interpretation]",
        "section": "translation",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Simultaneous and Consecutive Interpretation",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "THROUGHPUT VS LATENCY TRADEOFF:\n    The interpreter can trade latency for accuracy:\n    Increase lag (hold more input before producing output) →\n      better comprehension of full sentences (lower error rate)\n      but higher latency and higher M (memory load).\n    Decrease lag (stay close to the speaker) →\n      lower latency but higher error rate on long dependencies.\n    This is the classic throughput/latency tradeoff in\n    streaming systems: larger buffers → better batch decisions\n    but higher end-to-end latency."
    },
    {
      "id": "07-INTERPRETATION.md#028",
      "path": [
        "07-INTERPRETATION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:translation:07-interpretation, git-history:translation:07-interpretation]",
        "canonical_path": "translation/07-INTERPRETATION.md",
        "concepts": "[interpretation]",
        "current_path": "translation/07-INTERPRETATION.md",
        "id": "maxim:translation:interpretation",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "translation",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[interpretation]",
        "section": "translation",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Simultaneous and Consecutive Interpretation",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "COPING STRATEGIES AS SCHEDULING POLICIES:\n    Simplification → reduce work per unit (lower per-item cost)\n    Omission → drop items from the queue (priority scheduling)\n    Approximation → reduce precision requirement (lossy compression)\n    Delay → increase buffer size (larger working set)\n    These are exactly the strategies a scheduler uses when\n    demand approaches capacity: drop, simplify, or delay."
    },
    {
      "id": "07-INTERPRETATION.md#029",
      "path": [
        "07-INTERPRETATION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:translation:07-interpretation, git-history:translation:07-interpretation]",
        "canonical_path": "translation/07-INTERPRETATION.md",
        "concepts": "[interpretation]",
        "current_path": "translation/07-INTERPRETATION.md",
        "id": "maxim:translation:interpretation",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "translation",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[interpretation]",
        "section": "translation",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Simultaneous and Consecutive Interpretation",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "TRIGGERS FOR OVERLOAD ↔ SYSTEM LOAD SPIKES:\n    Dense information (numbers, proper names) →\n      spikes in M effort (each item requires held memory)\n      equivalent to a sudden burst of cache-miss-heavy requests\n    Long sentences requiring held memory →\n      working set overflow; items must be evicted before complete\n      equivalent to buffer overflow under sustained high throughput\n    Background noise →\n      increases L effort; equivalent to noise on a channel\n      requiring more processing per bit for error correction\n```"
    },
